<!-- ============================================================
     PROTOTYPE: Faded worked example (Pattern 6)

     Demonstrates: presenting a worked solution with algebraic
     blanks for the student to fill in. Each blank is an
     independent AlgEquiv input with its own PRT.

     Topic: Completing the square on x² + bx + c
     "Write x² + bx + c in the form (x + p)² + q"

     Key structural features:
     - Step-by-step solution in questiontext with [[input:]] placeholders
     - One PRT per blank (independent grading)
     - Wrong-answer feedback shows the specific step
     - Randomised coefficients with curated triples
     - generalfeedback shows the complete worked solution
     ============================================================ -->
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>PROTOTYPE: Faded example — completing the square</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[
<h4 class="tb-example">Example</h4>
<p>Write \({@expr@}\) in the form \((x + p)^2 + q\).</p>
<h4 class="tb-solution">Solution</h4>
<p>Half the coefficient of \(x\) is \({@bb@} \div 2 =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>So \({@expr@} = (x + {@ta1@})^2 - ({@ta1@})^2 + {@cc@}\)</p>
<p>\(= (x + {@ta1@})^2 -\) [[input:ans2]] \(+ {@cc@}\) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\(=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>
    ]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[
<p>Half the coefficient of \(x\) is \({@bb@} \div 2 = {@ta1@}\).</p>
<p>\[{@expr@} = (x + {@ta1@})^2 - ({@ta1@})^2 + {@cc@} = (x + {@ta1@})^2 - {@ta1^2@} + {@cc@} = {@completed@}\]</p>
    ]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <stackversion>
    <text>2024032401</text>
  </stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text>
/* Completing the square: x² + bx + c = (x + b/2)² + (c - b²/4)
   Curated triples [b, c] with integer b (even) for clean half-values. */
params: rand([[4, 1], [6, 2], [-4, 5], [8, 3], [-6, 1], [2, -3], [-8, 7], [10, 1]]);
bb: params[1];
cc: params[2];
expr: x^2 + bb*x + cc;
/* Teacher answers for the three blanks */
ta1: bb/2;
ta2: ta1^2;
ta3: (x + ta1)^2 + cc - ta2;
completed: ta3;
    </text>
  </questionvariables>
